  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><img height=\"161\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/92078ac0-9739-4e6c-93b4-9f9a0c24af39-image.png\" width=\"210\" /></p><p><img height=\"148\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/9d05804c-a746-4680-95f4-d83e5ca0ada4-image.png\" width=\"244\" /></p><p><img height=\"131\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/f2642e7d-54e2-46b5-b23a-62d71f3f922e-image.png\" width=\"230\" /></p><p><img height=\"185\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/211bcd8c-4626-4f86-b974-db6d6c68b0d9-image.png\" width=\"238\" /><br /><br />Chloroxylenol is a phenol derivative and hence, can be identified with <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>FeCl</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math> test.<br /><br />The primary amine of sulphapyridine can be identified with carbylamine test.<br /><br />The aliphatic alkyne of Norethindrone can be identified by the Baeyer&#39;s reagent.<br /><br />Penicillin gives test with sodium hydrogen carbonate.</p>",
